VALUES (4900932004020129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Microprocessor and Assembly Language Programming involves the syllabus topic microprocessor as applied within Evolution of Microprocessors, Microprocessor Bus organization, Operations of. Explain how microprocessor applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Microprocessor and Assembly Language Programming involves the syllabus topic marwadi university faculty of diploma studies information and communication technology a as applied within Instruction Set. Explain how Marwadi University Faculty of Diploma Studies Information and Communication Technology A applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Microprocessor and Assembly Language Programming involves the syllabus topic vectored interrupt. comparison of hardware and software interrupts. introduction to adva as applied within Interrupts concept and process, Classification of Interrupts, Interrupts Priorities,. Explain how Vectored interrupt. Comparison of hardware and software interrupts. Introduction to adva applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Microprocessor and Assembly Language Programming involves the syllabus topic features of arm processor. suggested text books / reference books: 1. microprocessor arc as applied within Differentiate between RISC and CISC processors, Intel’s advance processor,. Explain how Features of ARM processor. Suggested Text books / Reference books: 1. Microprocessor Arc applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** microprocessor appears in “Evolution of Microprocessors, Microprocessor Bus organization, Operations of”. Define its role and features, relate it to Memory: Classification and characteristics. 8085 microprocessor Architecture Introduction, features, Functional block diagram of 8085, Pin functions, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Memory: Classification and characteristics. 8085 microprocessor Architecture Introduction, features, Functional block diagram of 8085, Pin functions, Address. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Microprocessor and Assembly Language Programming task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Marwadi University Faculty of Diploma Studies Information and Communication Technology A appears in “Instruction Set”. Define its role and features, relate it to Marwadi University Faculty of Diploma Studies Information and Communication Technology Assembly Language Programming Basics, Classification of Instructions, Instruction Set, Instruction and data Formats, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Marwadi University Faculty of Diploma Studies Information and Communication Technology Assembly Language Programming Basics, Classification of Instructions, Instruction Set, Instruction and data Formats, Addressing Modes. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Microprocessor and Assembly Language Programming task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Vectored interrupt. Comparison of hardware and software interrupts. Introduction to adva appears in “Interrupts concept and process, Classification of Interrupts, Interrupts Priorities,”. Define its role and features, relate it to Vectored interrupt. Comparison of hardware and software interrupts. Introduction to advanced Processors, Interrupts concept and process, Classification of Interrupts, Interrupts Priorities,, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Vectored interrupt. Comparison of hardware and software interrupts. Introduction to advanced Processors, Interrupts concept and process, Classification of Interrupts, Interrupts Priorities,. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Microprocessor and Assembly Language Programming task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Features of ARM processor. Suggested Text books / Reference books: 1. Microprocessor Arc appears in “Differentiate between RISC and CISC processors, Intel’s advance processor,”. Define its role and features, relate it to Features of ARM processor. Suggested Text books / Reference books: 1. Microprocessor Architecture, Programming, and Application with the 8085 (9th edition), Gaonkar, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Features of ARM processor. Suggested Text books / Reference books: 1. Microprocessor Architecture, Programming, and Application with the 8085 (9th edition), Gaonkar, Ramesh. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Microprocessor and Assembly Language Programming task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

